, a n d
\mathrm{SUB}$ denote the compensation payable ratio, leverage, workforce education, R&amp;amp;D intensity, and subsidy intensity, respectively. The disturbance is assumed normal in the fitted Tobit likelihood. The reported estimates use observed-information-matrix standard errors. Firm and year effects are not separately estimated in this short panel. Coefficients refer to the latent outcome, not to marginal changes in observed efficiency; no average marginal effects are reported. Re-estimation after excluding 2025 assesses sensitivity to the observation period. It does not correct within-firm dependence, first-stage estimation uncertainty, endogeneity, or omitted common shocks. Those limitations delimit the inferential claims made below.
